Lets the core's offline page hold Chromium's auto-reload while a run of its game is going
(//browser_core/hooks.h), so a network that comes back mid-run doesn't throw the run away: the
page loads once the run ends. The page says it through Chrome's own channel for its game, the
error page controller's NetworkEasterEgg interface, which the browser takes only from the error
document in a tab's main frame. The auto-reloader gets a hold, which waits as a hidden tab's
reload waits; what holds it, and when, is the core's.

